    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361-a3">

                <pb facs="0471" n="375" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg375"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Auguste to Mr.
                            Terres.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Private Office of the Secretary of State of the
                                Interior</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                            Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1899-03-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 30,
                    1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. the Vice-Consul</hi>: On the request of the
                    chargé d’affaires of the Dominican Republic addressed to me, I would be greatly
                    pleased if you would have delivered Mr. Marcon Aroche (Alvarez) to the chief of
                    the post of Carrefour. Mr. Marcon Aroche, alias Alvarez, works at present in the
                    tobacco plantation that belongs to you and which you have established in that
                    quarter.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. Auguste.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
